--TEST--
`Core\Os` answers five facts about the host, each the shape its type promises, and `loadAverage` is the one a platform may keep nothing to answer from — `rule:core-api/tier-roster`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Every figure here differs on every machine this runs on, so what a case can
// pin is the shape and not the value. That is not a weak assertion: a member
// wired to the wrong primitive answers a zero, an empty string or nothing at
// all, and each of the five lines below is what refuses one of those.
uint $pid = Core\Os::pid();
if ($pid > 0) {
    echo "pid: a number\n";
} else {
    echo "pid: none\n";
}

string $host = Core\Os::hostname();
if (Core\Str::length($host) > 0) {
    echo "hostname: a name\n";
} else {
    echo "hostname: empty\n";
}

uint $cores = Core\Os::cpuCount();
if ($cores > 0) {
    echo "cpuCount: at least one core\n";
} else {
    echo "cpuCount: none\n";
}

// This is the *process's* resident set and never the request's held bytes,
// which are `Core\Budget`'s (ADR 0148 § 12). A running process holds memory,
// so a zero here is a member reading a counter nobody writes.
uint $resident = Core\Os::residentBytes();
if ($resident > 0) {
    echo "residentBytes: bytes held\n";
} else {
    echo "residentBytes: nothing\n";
}

// The one member with a platform that keeps nothing to answer from. Both arms
// print the same line on purpose: what this pins is that the member either
// answers three figures or says the platform has none, and never a plausible
// `[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]` a program would go on to act on.
try {
    var $load = Core\Os::loadAverage();
    if (Core\Arr::count($load) == 3) {
        echo "loadAverage: three figures or none\n";
    } else {
        echo "loadAverage: the wrong number of figures\n";
    }
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    if (Core\Str::contains($refused->message, "keeps no load average")) {
        echo "loadAverage: three figures or none\n";
    } else {
        echo "loadAverage: ", $refused->message, "\n";
    }
}
--EXPECT--
pid: a number
hostname: a name
cpuCount: at least one core
residentBytes: bytes held
loadAverage: three figures or none
